<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml v="1" site="svg-lab.custom" epoch="1">
  <head>
    <title>Inline SVG lab</title>
    <meta name="description" content="A div filled with inline SVG, not a stylesheet."/>
    <meta name="headline" content="A sealed page that draws its own gradient card with inline SVG."/>
    <meta name="author" content="Kickl demo"/>
    <meta name="date" content="2026-10-24"/>
    <meta name="location" content="screen one"/>
    <meta name="tags" content="svg, inline, sealed-pages, demo"/>
  </head>
  <body>
    <page>
      <h1>Inline SVG lab</h1>
      <badge>sealed page · inline svg · no css</badge>
      <p>This card is a div filled with an SVG fragment carried inside the sealed page.
      There is no stylesheet, no script, and no remote image request.</p>

      <html><![CDATA[
<center>
  <div>
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="720" height="220" viewBox="0 0 720 220">
      <defs>
        <linearGradient id="sunrise" x1="0%" y1="0%" x2="100%" y2="0%">
          <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#78c8c8" stop-opacity="1"/>
          <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#ff7a64" stop-opacity="1"/>
        </linearGradient>
        <linearGradient id="shade" x1="0%" y1="0%" x2="0%" y2="100%">
          <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#071016" stop-opacity="0"/>
          <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#071016" stop-opacity="0.62"/>
        </linearGradient>
      </defs>
      <rect x="0" y="0" width="720" height="220" rx="18" fill="url(#sunrise)"/>
      <rect x="0" y="100" width="720" height="120" rx="18" fill="url(#shade)"/>
      <circle cx="590" cy="78" r="42" fill="#fff3d6" opacity="0.9"/>
      <path d="M0 172 C120 128, 210 214, 340 166 S560 118, 720 158 L720 220 L0 220 Z"
            fill="#0b1b2c" opacity="0.72"/>
      <text x="28" y="58" fill="#071016" font-size="29" font-family="sans-serif"
            font-weight="bold">Inline SVG is the point.</text>
      <text x="30" y="86" fill="#071016" font-size="14" font-family="sans-serif">
        A div can be filled with drawing commands instead of a CSS layout system.
      </text>
      <text x="30" y="196" fill="#dbe7f3" font-size="12" font-family="sans-serif">
        sealed · jttp://svg-lab.custom/ · no scripts · no external requests
      </text>
    </svg>
  </div>
</center>
]]></html>

      <h2>What the renderer keeps</h2>
      <p>Static SVG shapes, gradients, text, paths, and data-URL images are rendered locally.
      Links and form controls are inert by construction. The package hash is verified before
      any of this drawing code reaches the view.</p>
    </page>
  </body>
</kml>
